/-!
# The coordinate cut of Stacks Tag 02NP: the twist is free, and the coordinates are finite

`Stacks.VeryAmpleAffineBase.ProjCoordinateCut` is the residue of [Stacks, Tag 02NP]: from an
immersion `α : X ⟶ Proj Γ(S, Sym(E))` over an affine base carrying the absolute degree-one twist
to `L`, it asks for an immersion into a finite-dimensional projective space over the base
carrying the hyperplane sheaf to `L`. This file spends two of its three parts.

* **The hyperplane sheaf costs nothing.** A finite family of global sections of an invertible
  module whose nonvanishing opens cover `X` defines a morphism `p : X ⟶ ℙⁿ_S` over `S`, pinned on
  each chart, and that morphism *already* pulls `𝒪(1)` back to the module: the twist
  identification is `Stacks.AmpleImmersionReduction.twistPullback`, which is
  unconditional. So the only thing a coordinate cut has to produce is a family for which `p` is
  an immersion.
* **The coordinates can be cut down to finitely many.** The graded ring
  `Γ(S, Sym(E))` is generated in degree one over its degree-zero part, so the standard opens of
  its degree-one elements cover `Proj`; `α` therefore factors through the degree-one open `U₁` of
  [Stacks, Tag 01N5], and `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismsIntoProj` makes
  `α⁎𝒪(1) ≅ L` globally generated by the sections attached to degree-one elements. Finite type
  over an affine base makes `X` quasi-compact, so finitely many of them suffice.

The third part is the immersion clause, isolated as
`Stacks.VeryAmpleAffineBase.ProjCoordinateImmersion` and spent in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/VeryAmpleAffineBase/CoordinateImmersion.lean`. The *choice* that
clause asks for — the finite affine cover, the algebra generators of each chart as fractions, and
the degree-one coordinates in which they are polynomials — is made in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/VeryAmpleAffineBase/CoordinateChoice.lean`; the docstring of
`ProjCoordinateImmersion` says how the clause follows from it.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.VeryAmpleAffineBase.ProjCoordinateImmersion`: **the immersion clause of the coordinate
  cut of Tag 02NP**, with the twist obligation discharged: a finite covering family of global
  sections of `L` whose pinned morphism to `ℙⁿ_S` is an immersion. It is proved in
  `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/VeryAmpleAffineBase/CoordinateImmersion.lean`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.VeryAmpleAffineBase.hasImmersionTwistOver_of_generatesStalks`: **a finite generating
  family of global sections of an invertible module whose pinned morphism is an immersion gives
  Tag 01VS's conclusion at that module.** No ampleness, no degree and no finite type hypothesis.
* `Stacks.VeryAmpleAffineBase.exists_generatesStalks_of_pullback_twistingSheaf`: **the cut to
  finitely many degree-one coordinates.** For `f` quasi-compact over an affine base and `L` the
  inverse image along any morphism to `Proj Γ(S, Sym(E))` of the absolute degree-one twist, `L`
  has a finite generating family of global sections.
* `Stacks.VeryAmpleAffineBase.projCoordinateCut_of_projCoordinateImmersion`:
  **`ProjCoordinateCut` from `ProjCoordinateImmersion`.**

## Implementation notes

The factorisation of `α` through `U₁` is `AlgebraicGeometry.IsOpenImmersion.lift`, whose range
hypothesis is free because `U₁` is all of `Proj`: degree-one generation of the section ring over
its degree-zero part is `Stacks.Tag01VMRelativeVeryAmple.adjoin_symAlgebra_eq_top`, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.iSup_basicOpen_eq_top'` turns it into the covering statement.

The family produced by `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismsIntoProj` is indexed by the whole
degree-one part of the Veronese subring, an infinite index type; the finite subfamily is extracted
by `IsCompact.elim_finite_subcover` and padded with the zero section to reach a `Fin (n + 1)`, as
`Stacks.ChartImmersionFinish.chartImmersion` does for the ample route.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02NP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02NP)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01N5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N5)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01N7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N7)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01VS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01VS)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

